# xreserve::mint_deny_guard
#
# FAUCET(01)-owned mint-deny guard (P5-01 R-MINT-16 slice): the ACTIVE mint policy of the faucet's
# TokenPolicyManager. The stock FungibleFaucet inherits `mint_and_send`, which routes through
# `policy_manager::execute_mint_policy` -> `dynexec` of the active mint-policy proc root
# (fungible.masm:248; policy_manager.masm:283). Registering this `check_policy` as that active root
# makes every stock `mint_and_send` against the faucet trap (ERR_XRESERVE_MINT_DENIED, R-MINT-16), so
# the CUSTOM `xreserve_mint` -- which bypasses the policy manager, calling kernel `faucet::mint`
# directly (xreserve_mint.masm:174) -- is the provably SOLE supply-increasing surface
# (INV-MINT-SECURITY, §5.2 COMPONENT-SPEC.md:271). Module home + flat path per D-1A
# (CANONICAL-OWNERSHIP-MAP.md:66). Loop history: crates/xusdc-encoding/TEST-LEDGER-01-MINT-SHELL.md.
#
# RED-GATE STATE (R-MINT-16 Step 0): `check_policy` ships with a NON-denying body
# (`push.0 assertz` = pass) so the executing-red gate observes `mint_and_send` reach success under an
# active-but-not-yet-denying policy; the deny test is then red on its exact-error assertion (a real
# MockChain execution reaching mint_and_send, not a compile error). Step 2 flips the single token
# `assertz` -> `assert` to make the guard deny. The `assertz` form references ERR_XRESERVE_MINT_DENIED
# so the constant is not unused under `with_warnings_as_errors`.

# ERRORS
# =================================================================================================

# R-MINT-16: the stock mint_and_send path is denied; only xreserve_mint may raise token_supply.
const ERR_XRESERVE_MINT_DENIED = "stock mint_and_send is denied; only xreserve_mint may raise supply"

# PUBLIC INTERFACE
# =================================================================================================

#! Mint policy that denies every stock `mint_and_send` request, forcing all supply increases through
#! the custom `xreserve_mint` surface. Registered as the ACTIVE mint policy of the faucet's
#! TokenPolicyManager; invoked by `policy_manager::execute_mint_policy` via `dynexec` on the stock
#! `mint_and_send` path. The custom `xreserve_mint` never routes here.
#!
#! Inputs:  [amount, tag, note_type, RECIPIENT]
#! Outputs: never returns -- unconditional trap (ERR_XRESERVE_MINT_DENIED); see RED-GATE STATE above.
#!
#! Invocation: dynexec
pub proc check_policy
    push.0 assertz.err=ERR_XRESERVE_MINT_DENIED
end
